diff --git a/docs/internationalization.md b/docs/internationalization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f63b56e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internationalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Languages
+
+Fizzy offers English (`en`, the default) and Japanese (`ja`). Open any application
+page with `?locale=ja` or `?locale=en` to choose a language. Unsupported and
+malformed values are ignored. Anonymous choices live in the Rails session; an
+authenticated choice is also saved on the global `Identity`, across accounts and
+future sign-ins. Signing out clears the browser session's choice, not the saved
+identity preference. A verified pending-login cookie can restore the preference
+on the verification-code screen before authentication finishes.
+
+Requests and mail deliveries use `I18n.with_locale`, restoring the previous locale
+even on exceptions. Mailers resolve the recipient's identity, not `Current.user`
+or the job worker's locale. Magic-link delivery can carry an explicit anonymous
+session choice. Japanese email links include `locale=ja`, including unauthenticated
+confirmation and unsubscribe links. Live broadcasts and push messages likewise
+use their recipient's preference.
+
+## Maintaining translations
+
+* Use `t` / `I18n.t` for application-owned text, including titles, placeholders,
+  confirmation prompts, accessibility labels, and native-bridge labels. The
+  matching English and Japanese catalogs are in `config/locales`.
+* Use interpolation for values, not translated sentence fragments where word
+  order matters. HTML translations use `_html` keys; user-provided values must
+  remain escaped. User-authored names, descriptions, and comments are not translated.
+* Use `l` / `I18n.l` for readable server dates; reserve `strftime` for machine
+  identifiers. JavaScript uses `helpers/i18n` and the document's translation
+  metadata, not the browser's language. Its English date format remains `en-US`.
+* Include `I18n.locale` in both fragment and collection cache keys (HTML and
+  JSON). Public pages vary by Cookie. Language switches invalidate offline
+  document caches and discard referrer labels from a different language.
+* Stored system comments remain canonical English for compatibility. Their
+  source event supplies localized presentation; historical comments without a
+  source-event reference are matched by timestamp and canonical body.
+* Static HTTP error pages cannot identify their viewer and contain both English
+  and Japanese, with language attributes on Japanese passages.
+* The rich-text editor's bundled JavaScript strings are intentionally unchanged.
+
+To add a language, supply complete catalogs, date formats, JavaScript messages,
+and its pluralization rule, then add it to `config.i18n.available_locales`.
+Production does not fall back to English for missing translations, and tests
+raise on missing translations.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+bin/rails db:migrate
+bin/rails test
+bin/rails test test/system/localization_test.rb
+```
+
+The regression tests cover persistence, clean-browser sign-in, malformed locales,
+locale isolation, every mailer, Japanese dates/plurals, accessibility, bilingual
+errors, shared caches, and live/push notifications.
